{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789308285,"nonce":"kewIeowP5j/Ws6VK7KjqmG9xHtU=","title":"bench/ash/dyn_dispatch: 4x slower than Ash's jit","message":"Mirror of Ash's BenchDynDispatch (checksum 1148967109). Per entity-iteration (1.28M): a polymorphic step(dt), a children() that allocates a small list, and a loop over it. Ash jit 0.05 s (Mac); NUC llvm at b4e5528: 0.20 s, GC 0.037 s.\n\nFindings so far:\n- run() failed its baseline compile ('undefined value') once constructor calls in a ternary became inline sites: loop versioning entered the copy without its merge blocks' values (398f0e2, fixed 64ffa18).\n- tick() never reached the top tier: the ceiling counted iterate/iteratorValue and inlinable calls as calls (b4e5528).\n- The iterate result was Num-guarded and deopted at every loop end; the whole body was recompiled unspeculated (b4e5528; the same deopt hit binary_trees' run()).\n- list.add through the generic wren_call_1: 2M calls; now an inline store when the buffer has room, the grow helper when not.\n- Every list cost a malloc for its elements and a free in the sweep's drop; a list allocated by the built-in heap now carries its first elements in its own allocation (8 for an empty literal, the exact count for a literal), growth moves them to a Buffer object in the heap when it fits a line, and only larger buffers fall back to malloc. NUC: a 1.28M-list loop 0.091 -\u003e 0.049 s, dyn_dispatch 0.20 -\u003e 0.18 s, GC 0.037 -\u003e 0.025 s. On the Mac the malloc share was larger.\n\nLeft: step(dt) and children() run through wren_known_call_N_nocheck (a helper that finds the jit slot and enters with a frame) rather than a direct call; Prop.children's list literal goes through wren_make_list plus one wren_list_add helper call per element; Mover.step and Prop.children stay in the Cranelift baseline (straight-line, ceiling Low) so tick's CHA guards enter baseline code.","files":null}]}